From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tntgdh-beep <tntgdh-beep@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: freezer: prevent spurious transition into non-frozen
 state

Backport of the cgroup v2 freezer fix that other LineageOS 4.19 kernels
already carry (LineageOS/android_kernel_qcom_sm8150, lineage-20, commit
7a05073b "UPSTREAM: cgroup: prevent spurious transition into non-frozen
state"). Neither android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8250 (lineage-24.0) nor
android_kernel_qcom_sm8250 (lineage-20) has it at the time of writing.

cgroup_leave_frozen() only decremented the frozen counter and cleared
current->frozen, and then relied on recalc_sigpending() to push the task
back into the signal handling loop. When leaving the frozen state races
with vfork() or do_signal_stop(), the cgroup can spuriously transition
to "unfrozen" while the task is still logically frozen. That task never
re-enters do_freezer_trap(), so it is left stuck and the whole system
hangs until the hardware watchdog reboots the device.

Instead, mark the task with JOBCTL_TRAP_FREEZE and raise TIF_SIGPENDING,
matching the upstream implementation, so the task is guaranteed to pass
through do_freezer_trap() before it can return to userspace.

Seen on elish (Xiaomi Pad 5 Pro, sm8250): opening Chrome eventually
freezes the whole system and the device reboots on the watchdog, with
"sysrq: Kill All Tasks" in the kernel log right before the reboot
(LineageOS issue #756 has the same symptom on a52q/a72q/gta4l).

Tested-on: elish, LineageOS 24.0-20261013-UNOFFICIAL, kernel
4.19.325-cip136-st20 (commit 6b34d2476532).
Signed-off-by: tntgdh-beep <tntgdh-beep@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 kernel/cgroup/freezer.c | 19 +++++--------------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/cgroup/freezer.c b/kernel/cgroup/freezer.c
index 3bfbb3c..c321e76 100644
--- a/kernel/cgroup/freezer.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/freezer.c
@@ -139,19 +139,13 @@ void cgroup_leave_frozen(bool always_leave)
 		cgroup_update_frozen(cgrp);
 		WARN_ON_ONCE(!current->frozen);
 		current->frozen = false;
+	} else if (!(current->jobctl & JOBCTL_TRAP_FREEZE)) {
+		spin_lock(&current->sighand->siglock);
+		current->jobctl |= JOBCTL_TRAP_FREEZE;
+		set_thread_flag(TIF_SIGPENDING);
+		spin_unlock(&current->sighand->siglock);
 	}
 	spin_unlock_irq(&css_set_lock);
-
-	if (unlikely(current->frozen)) {
-		/*
-		 * If the task remained in the frozen state,
-		 * make sure it won't reach userspace without
-		 * entering the signal handling loop.
-		 */
-		spin_lock_irq(&current->sighand->siglock);
-		recalc_sigpending();
-		spin_unlock_irq(&current->sighand->siglock);
-	}
 }
 
